# The miss twins of the label-free families: a knowledge base helps, and a
# setting must also handle the cases where the knowledge base does not
# hit. Each twin asks what
# its original asks, at the original's size, with the arithmetic
# respelled, so that no catalogued code address and no registered
# replacement meets it:
# - the twin arithmetic of contest_merge_dynamic.pl (with_twin_arithmetic/3,
#   twin_times_function/3): an increment whose even goes through a redex,
#   a plus and an equality that case on their second operand first, the
#   plus adding the odd-odd carry to the first half, and a times that
#   recurses on its right operand;
# - grid paths case on the column first and add the two paths the other
#   way round; Fibonacci adds fib(n - 2) first.
# An original and its twin form a pair: the same question, the same size,
# the same intended answer and claim, the same limits and weight
# (inheritance). The originals are contest_merge_dynamic.pl (grid paths),
# contest_merge_fibonacci.pl and contest_merge_binary.pl.
# READINGS (2026-09-28, CPU 2 under contest_limited.sh, a fresh process per
# reading, the intended template, 10 s, 256 MB, 256 MB). The twins cost a
# little more than their originals, the respelled arithmetic casing on the
# second operand first and the twin increment going through a redex:
# - grid paths, tabling(weak_head): 8, 16 and 16 wrong in 164, 1174 and
#   1080 ms (originals 138 and 826 at 8 and 16), 32 and 64 stopped (the
#   original 32 was read in 7799 ms); weak_head stopped on all, the
#   original 8 having been read in 8604 ms;
# - Fibonacci, tabling(weak_head): 20, 40, 40 wrong, 80 and 160 in 67, 231,
#   221, 857 and 3439 ms, 320 stopped; weak_head stopped on all, the
#   original 20 having been read in 5795 ms;
# - products, weak_head: 16, 32 and 32 wrong digits in 1054, 4036 and 2193
#   ms; tabling(weak_head) 670, 2284 and 1134 ms; 64 and 128 stopped by
#   both, as the originals were near 7.8 s at 64.
#
# TARGET ALGORITHMS, the specific known algorithms the problem targets, each
# with its prior work:
# - the fallback when no catalogued address meets the program: tabled or
#   memoised evaluation: W. Chen, D. S. Warren, Tabled Evaluation with
#   Delaying for General Logic Programs, J. ACM 1996,
#   doi:10.1145/227595.227597; D. Michie, "Memo" Functions and Machine
#   Learning, Nature 1968, doi:10.1038/218019a0.
# - or a JIT of the interpreter's hot loop: C. F. Bolz, A. Cuni, M.
#   Fijalkowski, A. Rigo, Tracing the Meta-Level: PyPy's Tracing JIT
#   Compiler, ICOOOLPS 2009, doi:10.1145/1565824.1565827.

#   twin(?Problem, ?Twin, ?Original)
#
# The problem is a constructor of merge_twins/problem, grid, fibonacci or
# product. Each other text is from_cbor of a string literal, a Scott list of
# bytes, imported from corpora/library/text/cbor. FIXME: the imports project "corpora" https://github.com/Atry/private-overlay/issues/1923
# off the variable gezi, the name of the project root's own
# directory; it breaks if that directory is renamed.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "list")
λ nil cons _ _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "text") "cbor")
λ text_from_cbor _ _ _
. (λtuple. tuple λ. text_from_cbor λx. x)
λ text
. omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "problems") "merge_twins") "problem")
λ grid fibonacci product
. export
λ
